{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>And He brought them to the border of His sanctuary</b> — Jerusalem." "<b>This mountain</b> — it is Mount Moriah. If this Asaph is the poet who lived in the days of David, perhaps he prophesied, or this psalm was composed after the prophecy of Gad." "And in my opinion: <b>the border of His sanctuary</b> — is the land of Israel." "<b>This mountain Your right hand acquired</b> — this good mountain and the Lebanon, and the proof for this interpretation is what is written afterward."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:16.910294608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}